Diamondhead has the power of crystallokinesis, allowing him to manipulate the crystals that [[Petrosapien (Classic)|his species]] are composed of: he has the power to summon formations of these crystals to erupt from underneath any ground surface.<ref name="EE">''[[Evil's Encore]]''</ref> He can control the rate and direction in which they grow or multiply to create various kinds of constructs, such as pillars or spikes. He can even make them levitate<ref name="VoV2" /> by controlling microscopic mineral particles in the air.{{Refn|[[:File:Diamondhead Alien Creation Card.png]]|group = Bandai|name = card}} Additionally, Diamondhead is capable of entrapping enemies in crystals, whether by trapping them through the ground,<ref name="ICW">''[[In Charm's Way]]''</ref> throwing crystals at them,<ref name="TH">''[[Trouble Helix]]''</ref> or by trapping them through touch,<ref name="TH">''[[Trouble Helix]]''</ref> and can generate crystals within objects and cause them to spike out, as demonstrated by [[Tetrax Shard (Classic)|Tetrax]] on an [[Attack Robot]].<ref name="SOTO">'''''[[Ben 10: Secret of the Omnitrix]]'''''</ref> Furthermore, Diamondhead's crystals can be made to completely block sonic attacks.<ref name="B10VtN10P1">''[[Ben 10 vs. Negative 10: Part 1]]''</ref>

Diamondhead has the ability to manipulate the structure of his physiology at will, allowing him to form structures on his own body, such as a large spike which was sharp enough to cleanly slice a falling tree in half,<ref name="ATTW10">''[[And Then There Were 10]]''</ref> or for protection, as demonstrated when Diamondhead formed crystals around the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] to stop [[Malware]] from grasping it.<ref name="TH" /> He can also use this technique to form his limbs into crystalline weapons such as blades,<ref name="MA">''[[Malgax Attacks]]''</ref> bludgeons,<ref name="GAGR">''[[Goodbye and Good Riddance]]''</ref> or a pickaxe, the latter demonstrated by [[Ultimate Kevin]].<ref name="NIBAC">''[[...Nor Iron Bars a Cage]]''</ref> Diamondhead's blades are sharp enough to cut through a cement truck in one swipe{{Refn|[[:File:Diamondhead Alien Creation Card OS.png]]|group=Bandai|name=card2}} or turn a car into confetti in a matter of seconds.{{Refn|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible}} Diamondhead can also alter the shape and size of his arms and hands, as demonstrated by [[Mad Ben]].<ref name="IaMBW1">''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 1]]''</ref> He can extend his arms very far, which allows him to create ramps for others or to propel himself upwards by pushing against the ground.<ref>''[[Blukic and Driba Go to Area 51]]''</ref><ref name="IaMBW1" /> He can also easily regenerate broken pieces of his body.<ref name="IWT" />

Diamondhead can fire crystal shards sequentially out of his hands.<ref name="Hunt">''[[Hunted]]''</ref><ref name="Vendetta">''[[Vendetta]]''</ref><ref name="IWT">''[[It Was Them]]''</ref> Usually, these shard projectiles are small, but Diamondhead can also fire out large chunks of crystals, as demonstrated by Mad Ben.<ref name="IaMBW1"/> They can also be thrown with such force that they explode on impact.<ref name="VoV2"/> Additionally, Diamondhead can remotely alter the shape of the crystals he produces to a very precise degree, allowing him to create spike clusters,<ref name="B10VtN10P1" /><ref name="CF">''[[Clyde 5]]''</ref> protective walls or shields,<ref name="EE" /> ramps of various curvature,<ref name="ACoF">''[[A Change of Face]]''</ref><ref name="ATTWB">''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref> moving platforms,<ref name="B10VtN10P1" /><ref name="K10" /><ref name="BA">''[[Ben Again]]''</ref> {{DreamInfo|or even a giant open hand to capture large falling objects,<ref name="PD">''[[Perfect Day]]''</ref>}} all by either summoning crystals from the ground, or sometimes by firing out shards that grow into which. He can summon crystals from the ground to trap his opponents by the feet.<ref name="TFBP1">''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]''</ref> Being that he can grow these with great speed, Diamondhead can stand on his emerging crystals to launch himself or opponents in the air<ref name="VoV2"/><ref name="CF" /> or to ride on like a board.<ref name="DAA">'''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]'''''</ref><ref name="CF" /> He can also surf with his crystals, materializing them from his hands.<ref name="TBoMB">''[[The Ballad of Mr. Baumann]]''</ref>

Apart from just forming weapons attached to his body, Diamondhead can also create independent, fully-formed crystal objects, such as an anchor on a chain,<ref name="B10VtN10P1" /> a shield,<ref>'''''[[Ben 10: Race Against Time]]'''''</ref><ref name="ATTWB" /><ref name="TEoaE">''[[The End of an Era]]''</ref> and a sword.<ref name="TTaC">''[[Third Time's a Charm]]''</ref><ref name="TEoaE">''[[The End of an Era]]''</ref>

Diamondhead's crystalline body resembles a living prism, allowing him to deflect most energy beams{{Refn|https://preservetube.com/watch?v&#61;no0FXNldzQA|group = CN}} up to and including the full energy of an orbital plasma cannon.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = card}} This allows him to render weapons similar to lasers useless by simply refracting.{{Refn|[[:File:Diamondhead's Powers.png]]|group = pop-up|name = DP}}<ref name="ATTW10" /> Similarly, rays generated by dimensional transporter devices will reflect off of Diamondhead's body.<ref name="HU">''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]''</ref><ref name="AD">''[[Arrested Development]]''</ref> In addition to refracting, Diamondhead can also absorb energy.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/a/ae/Vendetta_Script_As_Recorded.pdf ''Vendetta'' Script As Recorded]|group = script}}<ref name="Vendetta"/>{{Refn|[[:File:Diamondhead's Powers.png]]|group = pop-up|name = DP}}<ref name="ATTW10" /> However, there is a limit to the amount of energy he can absorb.{{Refn|[[:File:Diamondhead absorption is limited.png]]|group = DR}}<ref name="Vendetta"/> While Diamondhead was bonded with [[Crystalsapien (Classic)|Crystalsapien]] DNA, these absorption abilities were enhanced.{{Refn|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible}}

Diamondhead is quite strong,{{Refn|[[:File:Buzzshock Must Learn To Duplicate.png]]|group = MW}} strong enough to be a match for [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]] and his BFS,<ref name="HU"/> drag a cage holding a [[Gracklflint]] across [[Undertown]],<ref name="Rad"/> hold open [[Slamworm]]'s mouth,<ref name="IWT" /> and break his own crystals.<ref name="IaMBW1" /> He can also dig very well through solid surfaces by turning his arms into sharp spikes, seen when he unearthed [[Corrodium]] from under the floor of a building.<ref name="UW">''[[Under Wraps]]''</ref>

Due to the natural density of his crystalline body, Diamondhead is extremely durable; he withstood multiple blows and energy beams from Vilgax's large [[Mechadroid#Attack_Robots|Attack Robot Mechadroid]],<ref name="ATTW10" /> multiple punches from Four Arms,<ref name="Framed"/> survived the explosion of a factory at close range,<ref name="TUN">[[The Unnaturals]]</ref> took a blow from [[Sunder]]'s axe with just his hand (said axe effortlessly destroyed part of a large building),<ref name="SH">''[[Singlehanded]]''</ref> fell from the top of [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]]'s [[Charmcaster's Castle|castle]] after being hit by an energy beam from her and [[Michael Morningstar (Classic)|Michael]]'s combined strength,<ref name="CR">''[[Couples Retreat]]''</ref> and being punched by Vilgax in his [[Malware]] [[Malware Armor|armor]] from [[Galvan Prime (Classic)|Galvan Prime]] to [[Galvan B (Classic)|Galvan B]]. This incident also shows that Diamondhead can survive in the vacuum of space.<ref name="MA" />

Diamondhead can quickly burrow through the ground.<ref name="TBoMB"/>

Because he is made out of crystals that age very slowly, Diamondhead's body is very resistant to time rays that accelerate his aging. [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] learned this when being saved from [[Eon]]'s time rays by [[Ultimate Ben]] using Diamondhead's powers.<ref name="B10000R">''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]''</ref> Additionally, Diamondhead is immune to the acid from a [[Slammoid]].<ref name="IWT" />

Because Diamondhead is a super dense silicon-based alien, he is immune to [[Xenocite]] possession.<ref name="IM">''[[Inside Man]]''</ref> 

Diamondhead is resistant to fire and heat, such as that generated by a [[Pyronite (Classic)|Pyronite]], much like an ordinary diamond.<ref name="Framed"/> Diamondhead can also survive unscathed in magma.{{Refn|[[:File:Diamondhead Lava Resistance.png]]|group = DR}}

Diamondhead's eyesight is refractive.{{Refn|group=Bandai|name=card2}}

Diamondhead is able to spit out tiny sharp crystals from his mouth.<ref name="BWaV">''[[Back With a Vengeance]]''</ref><ref name="TSoC" />

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
TUS (298).png|Sonic Vibration Vulnerability
TSoC (156).png|Regeneration Limit
B10Mil (442).png|Immobilized due to Back Shards
TSoC (107).png|Affected by Cold Virus
</gallery>
Diamondhead is especially weak to sonic vibrations, such as from a [[Loboan (Classic)|Loboan]]'s sonic howls<ref name="K10">''[[Ken 10]]''</ref>, or an [[Ultimate Sonorosian]]'s [[Sonic Disc]]s,<ref name="TUS">''[[The Ultimate Sacrifice]]''</ref> both of which can render him unconscious. [[Tetrax Shard (Classic)|Tetrax]] also used a vibrating device to completely disassemble Diamondhead's body, although this left him conscious.<ref name="TSoC" />

If Diamondhead's body becomes completely disassembled, he is unable to regenerate himself.<ref name="TSoC" />

The two shards on Diamondhead's back can leave him stuck on a wall or on other surfaces that he gets knocked into.<ref name="B10000">''[[Ben 10,000 (Episode)|Ben 10,000]]''</ref> [[Gwen 10 (Gweniverse)|Gwen]] as Diamondhead, however, lacks this weakness.

Diamondhead can be trapped in crystal, as demonstrated by [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] using the [[Petropia Back-up Crystal]] to trap Tetrax.<ref name="TSoC" />

Though Petrosapiens normally resist the cold virus,<ref name="TSoC"/><ref name="TSoC" /> Diamondhead can be affected by it if the person transformed as him already has it.<ref name="TSoC" />

==History==
===Ben 10===
*Diamondhead first appeared in ''[[And Then There Were 10]]'', where he defeated [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]]'s large [[Mechadroid]] and saved a park.
*In ''[[Hunted]]'', Diamondhead did some training to master his powers. He was later defeated by [[Kraab (Classic)|Kraab]] and [[SixSix (Classic)|SixSix]] before being rescued by [[Tetrax Shard (Classic)|Tetrax]]. He then had a conversation with the latter until he reverted.
*In ''[[Secrets]]'', Diamondhead caught some criminals and appeared briefly while he was captured. Later, Diamondhead battled Vilgax on [[Mt. Rushmore (Classic)|Mt. Rushmore]] and was nearly defeated until the malfunctioning [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] made the former switch into [[Ghostfreak]]. 
** Also, Diamondhead appeared as one of the many alien templates used for Vilgax's army in an imaginary sequence.
*In ''[[The Big Tick]]'', Diamondhead failed to defeat the [[Great One]].
*In ''[[Framed]]'', Diamondhead fought [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]], in his [[Kevin's Framed Mutation|Framed Mutation]] as [[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]]. After Kevin escaped as [[Stinkfly (Classic)|Stinkfly]], Diamondhead fought some of [[Lt. Steel]]'s men until he reverted. Later, Kevin as Diamondhead battled Lt. Steel and [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] as [[Four Arms (Classic)|Four Arms]].
*In ''[[Grudge Match]]'', Diamondhead battled [[Kevin 11]] and defeated one of [[Slix Vigma]]'s robots.
*In ''[[Back With a Vengeance]]'', Diamondhead appeared four times. Firstly, Diamondhead was used by the Master Control. Secondly, he was used to find out which alien could spit the best loogie. Then, he was used to break out of Vilgax's grip. Lastly, Diamondhead prepared to fight both Kevin 11 and Vilgax, but was sucked into the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]] with them.
*In ''[[Midnight Madness]]'', a [[Sublimino|hypnotized]] Diamondhead was used off-screen to steal the motor to an amusement park ride.
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 (Episode)|Ben 10,000]]'', Diamondhead battled [[Vilgax (Original Future)|future Vilgax]].
*In ''[[A Change of Face]]'', Diamondhead tried to chase some criminals, but [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]] in [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]]'s body caught them instead.
*In ''[[Under Wraps]]'', Diamondhead made a hole for a fence post. He later dug up some [[Corrodium]] and fought the [[Mummy]] until he reverted.
*In ''[[The Unnaturals]]'', Diamondhead destroyed the [[Squires]] robots.
*In ''[[The Visitor]]'', Diamondhead helped fix the [[Rustbucket (Classic)|Rustbucket]].
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Secret of the Omnitrix]]''''', Diamondhead briefly appeared when the Omnitrix malfunctioned.
*In ''[[Perfect Day]]'', Diamondhead defeated SixSix and [[Vulkanus]] and mended a bus's tire for some cheerleaders in a dream.
*In ''[[Big Fat Alien Wedding]]'', Diamondhead defeated [[Camille Mann|Camille]]'s [[Camille's Ex-Boyfriend|ex-boyfriend]].
*In ''[[Ben 10 vs. Negative 10: Part 1]]'', Diamondhead slowed down the Rustbucket and fought [[Clancy]] and defeated [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]] and his [[Mutant Bat (Classic)|Mutant Bat]].
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]''''', Diamondhead appeared thrice. Firstly, Diamondhead attacked Ben in a dream. Later, Ben turned into Diamondhead to protect himself during a fall before the Omnitrix switched him into [[Four Arms (Classic)|Four Arms]]. Finally, Diamondhead frightened [[Sandra Tennyson|Sandra]] and [[Carl Tennyson|Carl]], reunited with [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] and [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and was ambushed and defeated by [[Azmuth's Father|Retaliator]].
*In ''[[Handle With Care]]'', Diamondhead stopped some museum thieves and tried to protect the once-stolen crystal eggs at the same time, but reverted before he could catch the falling eggs, thus breaking them.

===Five Years Prior to Omniverse===
*In ''[[Trouble Helix]]'', Diamondhead defeated [[Malware]].
*In ''[[Arrested Development]]'', Diamondhead caught a thief while unknowingly redirecting [[Billy Billions (Classic)|Billy Billions']] ray back at him.
*In ''[[Evil's Encore]]'', Diamondhead defeated several robot drones.
*In ''[[The Ballad of Mr. Baumann]]'', Diamondhead defeated [[Vulkanus]].

===Alien Force=== 
*Diamondhead was locked by the Omnitrix's reconfiguration in ''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 1]]''.
*In ''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]'', Diamondhead appeared after [[Chromastone (Classic)|Chromastone]] was destroyed by [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] and defeated the latter.
*In ''[[Singlehanded]]'', Diamondhead's hand was used by [[Julie Yamamoto|Julie]] to fight off [[Sunder]]. Meanwhile, Diamondhead broke a bridge in the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]] and fell off, forcing him to switch into [[Goop (Classic)|Goop]].
*In ''[[If All Else Fails]]'', Diamondhead battled the security of the [[Failsafe]]. He then tried to free [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]], but failed.
*In ''[[In Charm's Way]]'', Diamondhead fought off a [[Charmcaster (Classic)|mind-controlled]] [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] until he reverted.
*In ''[[The Secret of Chromastone]]'', Diamondhead was shattered by [[Tetrax Shard (Classic)|Tetrax]] in order to revive [[Sugilite]]. Later, Diamondhead restored [[Petropia (Classic)|Petropia]] with the [[Petropia Back-up Crystal]].
*In ''[[Vendetta]]'', Diamondhead was defeated by [[Ragnarok]].
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]'', [[Albedo|Negative]] Diamondhead defeated and captured Kevin and brought him to Vilgax.
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 2]]'', Diamondhead was briefly used by Vilgax's [[Bioid]]s.

===Ultimate Alien=== 
*In ''[[Basic Training]]'', Diamondhead defeated [[Brannigan]].
*In ''[[The Ultimate Sacrifice]]'', Diamondhead battled the [[Ultimate Forms#Sentient Forms|Sentient Ultimate Forms]], but was defeated by [[Sentient Ultimate Echo Echo]] and [[Sentient Ultimate Cannonbolt]].
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Diamondhead appeared thrice. Firstly, he fought [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]] before switching into [[Lodestar]]. Then, he deflected [[Dr. Caesar Salazar|Caesar]]'s [[Null Void Projector]] and drove off [[Alpha]]. Lastly, Diamondhead tried to battle Alpha again before he reverted back when Alpha copied the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]].
**Also, Diamondhead appeared as one of the many aliens seen when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was explaining his story to Rex.
*In ''[[Inspector 13]]'', [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] as Diamondhead used her Manna to save herself and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] as [[Jetray (Classic)|Jetray]] from a fall.
*In ''[[Couples Retreat]]'', Diamondhead fought [[Michael Morningstar (Classic)|Darkstar]] before switching into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]].
*In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', Diamondhead was seen confronting [[Albedo]] in a dream.

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[It Was Them]]'', Diamondhead fought [[Slamworm]].
*In ''[[Gone Fishin']]'', Diamondhead defeated [[Kork]].
*In ''[[Ben Again]]'', 16-year-old Diamondhead battled [[Eon]]. Later, Diamondhead was used by 11-year-old [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] in 16-year-old Ben's body to look at the top of a street light.
*In ''[[Rad]]'', Diamondhead dragged a cage with a [[Gracklflint]] in it across [[Undertown]] and met [[Rad Dudesman]].
*In ''[[A Fistful of Brains]]'', Diamondhead was defeated by [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Ultimate Humungousaur]].
*In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', Diamondhead appeared twice. Firstly, [[Gwen Tennyson (Gwen 10)|Gwen 10]] as Diamondhead was defeated by [[Eon]]. Later, [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]] as Diamondhead fought [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]].
*In ''[[Collect This]]'', Diamondhead stopped a gas truck knocked over by [[Slapstrike]] from crashing and exploding.
*In ''[[Blukic and Driba Go to Area 51]]'', Diamondhead battled [[Thunderpig]].
*In ''[[Clyde 5]]'', Diamondhead minimized the damage [[Clyde Fife|Clyde]] was causing until he reverted.
*In ''[[Stuck on You]]'', [[Skurd]] gave [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]] Diamondhead's arm and sword to fight [[Tyrannopede]].
*In ''[[The Secret of Dos Santos]]'', Skurd put an anchor made from Diamondhead's DNA in [[XLR8 (Classic)|XLR8]]'s tail to stop him.
*In ''[[Third Time's a Charm]]'', Skurd gave [[Kickin' Hawk]] Diamondhead's arm and sword to battle a dragon [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]].
*In ''[[Malgax Attacks]]'', Skurd used Diamondhead's shield while [[Blukic]] and [[Driba]] tried to remove him from the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]]. Later, Diamondhead fought [[Malware Armor|Mal]][[Vilgax (Classic)|gax]], but was defeated and punched from [[Galvan Prime (Classic)|Galvan Prime]] to [[Galvan B (Classic)|Galvan B]]. Lastly, Skurd put a shelter made from Diamondhead's DNA on [[Gravattack]]'s head to put [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] and [[Luhley]] inside as they escaped the self-destructing [[Chimeran Hammer (Classic)|Chimeran Hammer]].
*In ''[[The End of an Era]]'', Skurd gave [[Whampire]] Diamondhead's arm, sword, shield, and helmet to fight [[Exo-Skull]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Diamondhead appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

===[[Original Future Timeline|Original Future]]===
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 (Episode)|Ben 10,000]]'', Diamondhead fought [[Dr. Animo (Original Future)|Dr. Animo]] twice. He later battled [[Vilgax (Original Future)|Vilgax]] before switching 10-year-old [[Upgrade (Classic)|Upgrade]] into Cannonbolt and himself into [[Wildmutt]].
*In ''[[Ken 10]]'', Diamondhead fought [[Mot Snikrep]]. Later, Diamondhead was defeated by [[Kevin 11,000]].

===[[Ultimate Alien Future Timeline|Ultimate Alien Future]]===
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', [[Ultimate Ben]] used Diamondhead's crystal generation to save 16-year-old [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] from [[Eon]]. He later used Diamondhead's crystal projectiles to fight Eon.

===Gwen 10 (What-If?)=== 
*In ''[[Gwen 10 (Episode)|Gwen 10]]'', Diamondhead defeated [[Vilgax (Gwen 10)|Vilgax]]'s [[Mechadroid|large Mechadroid]] and saved a park.

===Goodbye and Good Riddance (What-If?)===
*In ''[[Goodbye and Good Riddance]]'', Diamondhead battled Vilgax's robots.

===[[Race Against Time Timeline]]===
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Race Against Time]]''''', Diamondhead fought Eon in the school gymnasium before hiding in the girls' changing room to avoid being seen by the other students until he reverted.

===Mad Ben's Timeline===
*In ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 1]]'', [[Mad Ben|Mad]] Diamondhead defeated [[Juryrigg]] and [[Rollaway]], but he accidentally freed [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]] and was defeated by [[Clockwork]].

